[[:db/retract 17592186198806 :question/answer-fields 17592186195554] [:db/retract 17592186198806 :question/answer-fields 17592186195549] [:db/retract 17592186198804 :question/answer-fields 17592186195536] [:db/retract 17592186198804 :question/answer-fields 17592186195530] [:db/retract 17592186198804 :question/answer-fields 17592186195527] {:db/id 17592186198312 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f87da9b9-2a22-52c7-9a6b-99820a90343e" "question-7a8d83c6-dbd1-545a-90aa-30ab2cbbb8f1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198173 :question/problem "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A = \\left[0,3\\right]?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $x_{\\max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if $x_{\\max} \\in S$ and $x \\leq x_{\\max}$ for all $x \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x_{\\min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if $x_{\\min} \\in S$ and $x_{\\min} \\leq x$ for all $x \\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(A) & =min[0,3]=0 \\\\ max(A) & =max[0,3]=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198313 :knowledge-point/title "Explaining the Existence of a Maximum or Minimum" :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f612405e-da38-57fe-9f2c-b87a69f932d8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198176 :question/problem "Given the set $S = (-\\infty,7],$ explain why $\\max(S) = 7.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $x_{\\max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if \n\n- $x_{\\max} \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x\\leq x_{\\max}$ for all $x \\in S.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $7$ is the maximum of the set $S$ because\n\n- $7 \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x \\leq 7$ for all $x \\in S.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198314 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f7921076-6399-562d-b241-b9adcf057407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198174 :question/problem "What are the maximum and minimum values of the set $A = \\{ n \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\mid \\: 3 \\lt n \\leq 8 \\}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- $x_{\\max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if $x_{\\max} \\in S$ and $x \\leq x_{\\max}$ for all $x \\in S,$ and\n\n- $x_{\\min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if $x_{\\min} \\in S$ and $x_{\\min} \\leq x$ for all $x \\in S.$\n\nNotice that the elements of the set can be listed as \n\n$$\nA = \\{ 4, \\: 5, \\: 6, \\: 7, 8\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum of the set equals $4,$ while the maximum of the set equals $8.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f87da9b9-2a22-52c7-9a6b-99820a90343e" :question/id #uuid "f87da9b9-2a22-52c7-9a6b-99820a90343e" :question/math-academy-id "q-181993" :question/problem "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $C={1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}?$\n\n$min(C)=$\n\n$-8$\n\n$\\,max(C)=$\n\n$7$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(C) & =min{1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}=-8 \\\\ max(C) & =max{1,\\,-8,\\,7,\\,2}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ac60a294-f5ef-5bf9-9f45-43037015447d" "answer-field-d9e539d9-f106-5c68-b7bd-8379f8454813"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ac60a294-f5ef-5bf9-9f45-43037015447d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac60a294-f5ef-5bf9-9f45-43037015447d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-eaaf3260-47f8-53f7-90b7-9fe5eef20f3f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eaaf3260-47f8-53f7-90b7-9fe5eef20f3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eaaf3260-47f8-53f7-90b7-9fe5eef20f3f" :answer/id #uuid "eaaf3260-47f8-53f7-90b7-9fe5eef20f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d9e539d9-f106-5