{x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $-2\\notin A$ and $1\\notin A.$ So, we have the following:\n\n- $min(A)=min(-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$\n\n- $max(A)=max(-2,1),$ which $\\text{does not exist}$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-74395e94-562b-504b-9894-269851b33c1e" "answer-field-52767750-0e81-5c56-bf4b-19800c3813fb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-74395e94-562b-504b-9894-269851b33c1e" :answer-field/id #uuid "74395e94-562b-504b-9894-269851b33c1e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-be92b7b6-3dac-5535-9707-0581d17d1233" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be92b7b6-3dac-5535-9707-0581d17d1233" "answer-84090c20-f276-5fcf-9782-eeea0509bf68" "answer-07ae3505-017e-5176-98d8-cce3fcb6b043"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be92b7b6-3dac-5535-9707-0581d17d1233" :answer/id #uuid "be92b7b6-3dac-5535-9707-0581d17d1233" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84090c20-f276-5fcf-9782-eeea0509bf68" :answer/id #uuid "84090c20-f276-5fcf-9782-eeea0509bf68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "equals $-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07ae3505-017e-5176-98d8-cce3fcb6b043" :answer/id #uuid "07ae3505-017e-5176-98d8-cce3fcb6b043" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "equals $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-52767750-0e81-5c56-bf4b-19800c3813fb" :answer-field/id #uuid "52767750-0e81-5c56-bf4b-19800c3813fb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cb1c9689-e444-5074-a133-a959b46da192" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cb1c9689-e444-5074-a133-a959b46da192" "answer-207759b6-182c-55f0-9c5e-c12414cb8089" "answer-77292180-bab4-528b-8825-f3bc300eaa12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb1c9689-e444-5074-a133-a959b46da192" :answer/id #uuid "cb1c9689-e444-5074-a133-a959b46da192" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "does not exist" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-207759b6-182c-55f0-9c5e-c12414cb8089" :answer/id #uuid "207759b6-182c-55f0-9c5e-c12414cb8089" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "equals $-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77292180-bab4-528b-8825-f3bc300eaa12" :answer/id #uuid "77292180-bab4-528b-8825-f3bc300eaa12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "equals $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186199565 :tutorial/content "The **minimum** of a set $S$ is the element $x_{\\min} \\in S$ such that \n\n$$\nx_{\\min} \\leq x\n$$\n\nfor all $x \\in S.$ In other words, the minimum is the element of $S$ that is *smaller than or equal to* any other element.\n\nSimilarly, the **maximum** of a set $S$ is the element $x_{\\max} \\in S$ such that \n\n$$\nx \\leq x_{\\max}\n$$\n\nfor all $x \\in S.$ In other words, the maximum is the element of $S$ that is *larger than or equal to* any other element.\n\nFor example, what are the minimum and maximum of the following set? \n\n$$\nA = \\big\\{ 2, \\: -\\sqrt{5}, \\: 3, \\: -1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nNote that $-\\sqrt{5} \\approx -2.236.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(A) & =min{2,\\,-\\sqrt{5},\\,3,\\,-1}=-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ max(A) & =max{2,\\,-\\sqrt{5},\\,3,\\,-1}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSome sets may not have a maximum or minimum. \n\nFor example, consider the semi-open interval of real numbers $B=[1, 5).$ In this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\min(B) = \\min[1, 5) = 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, since $5 \\notin B,$ the set has no maximum!\n\nFinally, note the following:\n\n- The maximum and minimum elements *must* belong to the underlying set.\n\n- If the maximum or minimum elements exist, they are unique. In other words, there can be, at most, only one maximum and only one minimum.\n\n- If the \"less than or equal to\" operation is not defined *for all* elements of a set $S,$ then the set has no maximum or minimum. For example, the following set has no minimum and maximum:\n\n$$\nS = \\big\\{\\mathbb R, \\clubsuit, 2, 3, \\langle 1, 2, 3\\rangle \\big\\}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]}]
